    "result_text": "The full build passes. \n\n## Summary\n\nThe spec required the owner response to expose a `selfLink` = `/api/owners/` + the owner's id. The `AcceptanceTest` creates an owner then reads it back via `GET /api/owners/{id}` and asserts `$.selfLink`, so the field belongs on the owner response DTO, not just the create endpoint.\n\nI made two small, focused changes:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `selfLink` string property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` carries the field (and it's documented consistently with the other derived fields).\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a `@Mapping(target = \"selfLink\", ...)` plus a small `selfLink(Owner)` helper that returns `\"/api/owners/\" + owner.getId()` (null before an id is assigned). This centralizes the derivation in the mapper alongside the other derived fields, so every response path (GET, create, update, list) gets it for free without duplicating the logic in each `RespondWith*` function.\n\nBoth the `AcceptanceTest` and the full test suite are green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0).",
